Re-enable the D3D shared-image pipeline for the MinGW build.

The QtWebEngine compositor in this tree always sets the SCANOUT shared-image
usage on Windows (native_skia_output_device.cpp:259, gated by
m_isNativeBufferSupported which defaults to true and is only overridden for
Ozone). On Windows only DCompImageBackingFactory and D3DImageBackingFactory
can satisfy that usage, but 0008-chromium-gpu.patch gates them on
BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC) / `if (is_msvc)`, so under MinGW none of them register.
Result: shared_image_factory.cc:904 logs

  Could not find SharedImageBackingFactory with params: usage:
  Gles2Read|DisplayRead|DisplayWrite|Scanout, format: RGBA_8888 ...

on every frame, the GL/Skia context is marked lost, and the QtWebEngineWidget
shows nothing. The Windows OpenGL/D3D11/Vulkan device classes also call
m_frontBuffer->overlayImage() unconditionally, so dropping SCANOUT alone is
not a workable fix - the D3D pipeline itself has to be present.

This patch:
 * In gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn, merges the post-0008 `is_mingw`
   and `is_msvc` blocks back into a single `is_win` block so the d3d_*,
   dcomp_*, dxgi_swap_chain_* and dxgi_shared_handle_manager sources are
   compiled for MinGW too. MSVC-only `.lib` link names stay under is_msvc.
 * Reverts every BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC) site introduced by 0008 back to
   BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) so D3DImageBacking::UpdateExternalFence,
   SharedImageBacking::UpdateExternalFence, the Win-only methods on
   SharedImageInterface / SharedImageManager / shared_image_stub,
   GLTextureImageBacking::ProduceVideo, and the factory registrations all
   compile and run for MinGW.

GN settings unrelated to the D3D shared-image pipeline (e.g. /DELAYLOAD,
/IGNORE:4217, MinGW-only `#if defined(__MINGW32__)` workarounds, _uuidof ->
__uuidof) are deliberately untouched.

This is a "starter" patch: with the D3D path enabled, MinGW compile errors
in d3d_image_backing.cc / d3d_shared_fence.cc / dcomp_*.cc are expected.
mingw-w64 ucrt64 has gained ID3D11Fence/ID3D11Device5 in d3d11_4.h and a
working dcomp.h since 0008 was authored, so most should be tractable.

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn b/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
@@ -606,17 +606,7 @@ target(link_target_type, "gles2_sources") {
     }
   }
 
-  if (is_mingw) {
-    # The D3D shared-image backing pipeline (d3d_image_backing.cc,
-    # dxgi_shared_handle_manager.cc, dcomp_*) is built only under is_msvc
-    # because it pulls in d3d_shared_fence and DComp APIs that don't compile
-    # with MinGW headers. d3d_image_representation.cc cannot stand alone
-    # without those backing definitions, so it is excluded here too.
-    libs = [ "dxguid", "dxcore" ]
-    all_dependent_configs = [ ":service_win_linker_flags" ]
-  }
-
-  if (is_msvc) {
+  if (is_win) {
     sources += [
       "dxgi_shared_handle_manager.cc",
       "dxgi_shared_handle_manager.h",
@@ -639,11 +629,17 @@ target(link_target_type, "gles2_sources") {
       "shared_image/dxgi_swap_chain_image_representation.cc",
       "shared_image/dxgi_swap_chain_image_representation.h",
     ]
-    libs = [
-      "d3d12.lib",
-      "dxguid.lib",
-      "onecore.lib",
-    ]
+    if (is_msvc) {
+      libs = [
+        "d3d12.lib",
+        "dxguid.lib",
+        "onecore.lib",
+      ]
+    } else {
+      # MinGW uses bare lib names; onecore is part of -lkernel32 transitively
+      # via the toolchain config, so we only need d3d12/dxguid/dxcore here.
+      libs = [ "d3d12", "dxguid", "dxcore" ]
+    }
     all_dependent_configs = [ ":service_win_linker_flags" ]
   }
 }
